===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*terkʷ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|-}}, from {{der|en|LL.|torsio|torsio, torsionem}}, from {{der|en|la|tortio}}, from {{m|la|torqueō||twist, turn}}. See {{m|en|torture}}, {{m|en|-tort}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɔː.ʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-torsion.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtor.ʃɪn/|/ˈtor.ʒɪn/|/ˈtor.ʃən/|/ˈtor.ʒən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of [[turn]]ing or [[twist]]ing, or the state of being twisted; the twisting or [[wrench]]ing of a body by the [[exertion]] of a [[lateral]] [[force]] tending to turn one [[end]] or part of it about a [[longitudinal]] [[axis]], while the other is [[hold|held]] [[fast]] or turned in the opposite direction.
# {{lb|en|math}} {{rfdef|en}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} {{rfdef|en}}<!--The given definitions are pretty outdated too - all from Webster's 1913 dictionary. Good luck, Kikiman, lots of love, Wonderfool. :)-->
# {{lb|en|mechanics}} That [[force]] with which a [[thread]], [[wire]], or [[rod]] of any [[material]] [[return]]s, or tends to return, to a state of [[rest]] after it has been [[twist]]ed; [[torsibility]].
# {{lb|en|surgery}} The [[stop]]ping of [[arterial]] [[haemorrhage]] in certain cases, by [[twist]]ing the [[cut]] [[end]] of the [[artery]].

